--- a/hw/vfb/man/Xvfb.man
+++ b/hw/vfb/man/Xvfb.man
@@ -70,6 +70,15 @@
 This option only exists on machines that have the mmap and msync system
 calls.
 .TP 4
+.B "\-listenfd \fIdescriptor\fP"
+This option makes the already open, listening socket \fIdescriptor\fP the
+server inherited (for example a Unix socket its parent bound to a file in a
+private folder) the server's only listener: no other listening socket is
+created, as with \fB\-nolisten\fP for every transport, and no lock file.
+Clients connect with \fBDISPLAY\fP set to the socket's path. The server
+never removes the socket's file. The server's own \fBDISPLAY\fP must not
+name that path.
+.TP 4
